        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The continuation of government operations depends on passing a continuing resolution.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Avoiding a government shutdown is a desirable outcome for the speaker and their audience.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Political cooperation visible in public appearances reflects genuine consensus behind closed doors.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker trusts media coverage and public reporting as reliable indicators of political dynamics.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 90728,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90728.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's important for us to be able to fund programs that are essential to the people we represent. I think it's great to have the internal debate. But at the end of the day, and you and I have talked about this before, I always like to talk about it as kitchen table economics. We all have sat down. You know, mom and dad sat down, they got the checkbook out. And they always had priorities of what it is that they wrote a check for. Right now, there are programs that are essential to the people that we represent that make sure that those programs still get funded. All the CR does, which we've heard of these things. Everybody uses acronyms today.",
