    "turn_text": "get in a fight, are they really going to be standing here with us? Or are we what the term are leading from behind? I don't think makes sense. But that was a statement that was put out years ago. I don't think we want to leave from behind. We want, America has to stand strongest and straightest and upright at all times and we have to defend ourselves. So that's 14 cents out of that dollar. Now we come down to 13 cents. So if you're sitting at the kitchen table and you're looking at what you have left now, you're really got to take a look at where am I spending this money? Where is the best return on it for my family, for my district, for my country? And that's where the hard things come up. And we start to talk about different programs. And now it's like, well, you've got to be careful what you cut. You've got to be careful on who you no longer support on people who were Relying on that support never thought it would go away. What are we doing to the people we represent? It's the hardest job I've ever had when I had, you know, when I was running my own business, I was concerned about everybody. But at the end of the day, I had to do things to keep us viable and keep the business open. And so I would make those decisions. One of the things I never touched was salaries or benefits to the people that I work with every day to have some success. So I try to look at this the same way. What are we doing? And how are we supporting the most vulnerable in our society? And then secondly, the people that we have made commitments to, that we can, if we walk away from that, then we're no longer who we say we are. And that is the greatest country, the greatest nation the world has ever known. It is those who are most vulnerable that need our help. Now we come down to all those different programs. How do you divvy that up? And that's where the conversation takes place. Although I got to tell you, as a parent of four children, as a grandfather of 10 children, And as somebody who was raised in a big family and has always been on parts of teams, never the stand out on it, but somebody who was good at supporting the rest of the team, I really start to wonder at what point is that we stop positioning ourselves for time on TV and start positioning ourselves for what is it that the people in our district sent us to do and a lot of it is concerned to forget the politics of it. I mean that sincerely. Look at the policy. We have got to make sure that our policy is rock solid and that when we tell somebody something, we keep our word. We don't take things from them.",
