    "turn_text": "that is that it goes back to day one. Why we even had a federal government. Why it was so important to have an army that could defend our shores and make sure that we were safe. If we walk away from the most basic of what our responsibilities are as a federal government, then we've walked away from what the founders put into place. And as I just said, what one and a half million men and women died, died for it. We have always been the first to show up when there's a problem somewhere in the world. And we, and we, yet if we look at our own homeland and we're saying, well, I mean, really are okay. Our borders are okay. No, they're not. They're not okay. They're not being defended the right way. The border control men and women. are absolutely exhausted, underfunded, and undermanned. We have to make sure that our borders, first, my first obligation is to the American people and making sure that they're secure.",
