    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Yeah. Well, I mean, look, we know the immigration now has become a national concern for several years. It was like, no, there's really no problem done there. We're starting to see it. Every one of our states is a border state. There were people coming into our states that have not been vetted yet. We don't really know what their long range plans are. We are the most welcoming people in the world and the person to show up anytime there's a crisis anywhere. I mean, I'm not questioning America's resolve and the way we believe. But I do know this. So there's something wrong when the basics of how it is that we were formed, of what our Constitution guarantees. When we don't know that, but we go off of bits and pieces that we pick up that seem clever at the time to say, when we forget that our number one responsibility is the defense of our homeland. And the rest of it is all important. I'm not saying it's not, but I'm just saying it's the American people. And I believe the most famous line in any movie I've ever watched is in a movie with Jack Nicholson called Up You Good Men",
